# Fly To Coords puts the vehicle in Guided and sends it the typed position, as setGuidedModeWP does.
#
# flyToCoordsToolStripMenuItem_Click reads 'lat;long;alt' (each a float), and setGuidedModeWP asks
# for Guided when the vehicle is not in it - DO_SET_MODE, then SET_MODE twice - and sends
# SET_POSITION_TARGET_GLOBAL_INT with the C#'s mask, 0xFDF8, in the relative frame. SITL accepts
# Guided while disarmed and ignores the target on the ground, so nothing moves.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:6052-6122, ExtLibs/ArduPilot/Mavlink/MAVLinkInterface.cs:4423-4551`
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-flytocoords.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 10

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

# Out of Guided first, so the mode request is part of what is sent.
click Stabilize
expect vehicle.mode Stabilize

click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-flytocoords
expect fly.prompt Please enter the coords 'lat;long;alt' or 'lat;long'
# The minus as a key: `xdotool type -35...` would read the text as an option.
key minus
type 35.3625;149.1657;20
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM: gpui forwards every
# key press to it and handles the key when it comes back), while a click is handled as it
# arrives. Clicking OK straight after typing nineteen characters answered "no guided height,
# latitude or longitude yet" - the refusal for a lat;long with no height, which flies at
# GuidedMode.z, zero: the box held a prefix such as "-35.3625;149.1657" when the click overtook
# the rest. So wait, and check the box holds the whole text before answering it.
expect fly.prompt.value -35.3625;149.1657;20
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent ~ SET_POSITION_TARGET_GLOBAL_INT frame=3 mask=0xFDF8 lat=-3536249
expect fly.sent ~ alt=20
expect fly.ack ~ MAV_CMD_DO_SET_MODE:
expect vehicle.mode Guided
expect fly.guided.frame 3

# Cancelling sends nothing: the empty text is Invalid Field, as in the C#.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-flytocoords
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.sent nothing: Invalid Field

# Put the mode back for whatever runs next.
click Stabilize
expect vehicle.mode Stabilize
